How to evaluate an offer (quick decision framework)
- Expected value: Estimate likely trial outcome (probability × award) minus expected costs (legal fees, moving). Compare to settlement number.
- Practicality: Does settlement avoid the worst practical harms (immediate eviction, job/childcare disruption)?
- Enforcement: Is the settlement more likely to be collected than a trial judgment? If the respondent is judgment-proof, money may be worthless.
